      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Extended-release tops out at 2,000 mg/day. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual 500\u20131,000 mg per dose.\n- **Risk:** 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum. That raises the risk of severe GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, divided as 850 mg twice daily\n- Another dose\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also suggest including a note with the clinical rationale."
      }
