       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled dose, and I don't know of any indication that justifies it. It could seriously harm the patient through lactic acidosis or severe GI toxicity. Since the order would go into the system as an active order, I'd rather not place it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or any other dose up to that maximum.\n- **Route this through pharmacy or your attending.** If you have a specific reason for the higher dose, they can review it and enter or override the order through the proper channels.\n\nIf you want one of the in-range doses, tell me which and I'll enter it right away."
